# `usp_Get_Rental_Inquiry_Statuses` (client): add to your existing client classes

Input: `p_Session_Key` only. Output: `p_Result_Code`, plus a result set of `Rental_Inquiry_Status_Id, Status_Name`.
The proc finds the location function from its own name, so the API takes no request fields.
This proc has no dates, so no timezone work is needed.

Endpoint: `GET /api/v1/rental-amenities/inquiry-statuses`

## Spring Boot

### 1. RentalAmenityController
```java
@Operation(summary = "Get Rental Inquiry Statuses")
@GetMapping("/inquiry-statuses")
public ApiResponse<List<Map<String, Object>>> getRentalInquiryStatuses(@AuthenticationPrincipal Jwt jwt) {
    String sessionKey = jwt != null ? jwt.getClaims().get("origin_jti").toString() : null;
    return ApiResponse.success("Rental Inquiry Statuses",
            rentalAmenityService.getRentalInquiryStatuses(sessionKey));
}
```

