### 4. RentalAmenityDao
Use the BaseDao method that returns a list. `executeList` is a placeholder, as in the earlier get API.
```java
// client1.usp_Get_Rental_Inquiry_Statuses
public List<Map<String, Object>> getRentalInquiryStatuses(String sessionKey) {
    Map<String, Object> params = new HashMap<>();
    params.put("p_Session_Key", sessionKey);
    return executeList("usp_Get_Rental_Inquiry_Statuses", params);   // p_Result_Code validated in BaseDao
}
```

`TicketRequest` needs no change here. I pass the session key as a plain string because the API has no other input.
If you want the same shape as your other methods, build a `TicketRequest`, call `setSessionKey` on it, and pass that.

